  "principle": "The deterministic-replacement REGISTRY (the moat): real, pluggable tools per tool-plane that the supervisor selects from to compile a capability down to the cheapest bounded path. Populates the planes that lack a dedicated registry (OCR→ocr_provider_registry, browser→web_browsing_stack_registry, llm→model_index already cover theirs). Every tool is a CANDIDATE (serves_truth=false; discovery≠trust); license_class/vendorable are derived by src/openharnesshub/licenses.classify_license — COPYLEFT (AGPL/GPL/MPL) + NON-COMMERCIAL + UNSTATED are technique-only (study clean-room, never vendor). A new tool drops in as a row, zero caller change. Grows toward hundreds via the discovery flywheels.",
